{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Types of Software  "}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear about computer software. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understands systems theories, business processes and basic concepts on IT.  Create a map of processes that allows identifying areas in an information system, using IT tools to generate reports based on the company's needs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level. Exchanges simple information on IT concepts, systems theory, and diagrams of processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present Tense - Interrogative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span> tense is used to talk about ideas or situations that are routines or habits. Also, it can be used to talk about ideas that are true now. These ideas are generalizations about people or things, or it can be beliefs as well."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In simple words, what does computer software mean?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do we speak the same language as computers?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In order to make <span class=\"strong\">questions</span> in using the <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span>, you have to use the auxiliary verbs <span class=\"strong\">do</span> or <span class=\"strong\">does</span>. You can use short answers. <br/> <br/> Structure of <span class=\"strong\">yes/no questions:</span> <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">Do/Does</span> + subject + <span class=\"strong\">verb</span>?</div><br/><br/>  Example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Do</span> you <span class=\"strong\">use</span> programming tools at work?</span><br/><br/> When you want to make <span class=\"strong\">information</span> or <span class=\"strong\">wh- questions</span> in <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span>, you need to use <span class=\"strong\">what, where, when, who, which, whose</span> or <span class=\"strong\">how</span> before the auxiliary verbs <span class=\"strong\">do</span> or <span class=\"strong\">does</span>. <br/><br/> Structure of <span class=\"strong\">wh- questions</span> <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">Wh- question word </span> + <span class=\"strong\">do/does</span>+ subject +<span class=\"strong\">verb</span>?</div> <br/><br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What does </span> JAVA <span class=\"strong\">stand for</span>?</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Check a computer with the typical programs and functions and analyze them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of the programs you can recognize on it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Classify the programs into the 3 kinds of software."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your list to the class."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I analyze the programs in a computer."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I list the programs in a typical computer."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I classify the software programs according to the type."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present and explain my work to the class."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What Is Software?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A software or computer software includes programs and applications that a computer uses in order to process information or perform a task. It is made of encoded information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The basic types of software are: <br> <br>  1. Application software. They are called domain of use. They are the productivity programs because they enable the user to complete a task. For example, a word processor. <br> <br>  2. System software. They are called domain of execution. These programs manage the computer. For example, an operating system like Windows or Linux. <br> <br>  3. Programming tools. These programs support and manage the computer. They also diagnose and fix problems."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "With this in mind "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "taking this into account"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrase)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: With this in mind, we need to remember that if we want a computer to do something, we need to translate the command we give so a computer can understand it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob02aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "translate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to convert one language into another"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need to translate the command we give so a computer can understand it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "command"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an instruction or order "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need to translate the command we give so a computer can understand it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "add"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put in something in order to make it grow"}, {"t